Experimental variables
  Started at:          2026-10-13T10:35:56.782Z
  Network:             hoodi (chainId 560048)  RPC https://ethereum-hoodi-rpc.publicnode.com
  Block timing:        network (~12000 ms)
  Block gas limit:     60,000,000
  Contracts:           Chain 0xAa5FDAB5D55D76da97C15D435f5b0C059e72BF07, GlobalReputation 0x2785120d91f169F7d6B196a35730206Bf7fa681f
                       Storage 0x56bAA20bE01075979A598acD02f666fAeA14e7d7, StealthAnnouncer 0xe4D8ebC06747594C6F7c3F9f414f89fD058Ae457
  Tree:                note tree depth 25; every past root stays valid (mapping, O(1)). Ratings: Chain.rateOrder, in the clear
  Privacy:             stealth address derived and announced per order, stipend in makeOrder, stealth wallet sends poolWithdraw/prepareOrder/pickupOrder/rating (legacy gasPrice), one real Groth16 proof per cycle (the withdrawal)
  Concurrency levels:  {1, 2, 4, 8} clients; units per client: makeOrder 2, cycle 2
  Client model:        closed loop (next tx after the previous receipt), clients start together
  Prover:              snarkjs 0.7.6 groth16.fullProve, 1 concurrent proofs on 16 CPUs (12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-12500H)
  Receipt polling:     1000 ms
  Host:                Node v20.20.2 on linux x64

Definitions
  window      wall clock from the level start to the last receipt of the level
  units/s     completed units (orders or cycles) / window;  tx/s = mined transactions / window
  unit lat.   one unit's wall clock (makeOrder: derivation + announce + makeOrder; cycle: all its steps)
  incl. lat.  sendTransaction returned -> block containing the tx observed
  blk/util    blocks spanned by the level / mean and max gasUsed/gasLimit over those blocks
  root age    note-tree insertions between a withdrawal proof's snapshot and its on-chain check
              (every past root stays valid: mapping, O(1)); stale = proofs regenerated because the dry run
              reported their root as not known

